namespace TiaMcpServer.Plc;

/// <summary>
/// The plc_read and plc_write tool descriptions (K91). The tool listing carries only the short descriptions, which name
/// every operation and the safety rules; the full per-operation reference (<see cref="PlcOperationReference"/>) is served
/// by plc_read describe_operations, because the full texts made Claude Desktop refuse both tools ("Claude can't use 2
/// tools from Tia portal").
/// </summary>
internal static class PlcToolDescriptions
{
    internal const string Read = "Run up to 50 PLC read operations in one call against the verified bound project; reads run independently, so a failing item does not stop later ones. Each item is { operationId, operation, ...fields } and takes only its operation's fields. describe_operations (optional operationNames: 1 to 3 PLC read or write operation names per item, several items per call; needs no bound project) returns each named operation's required and optional fields, the full field rules and its reference text; without operationNames it lists every plc_read and plc_write operation with its fields and the tool-wide rules. Call it before using an operation whose fields you do not know. Content reads return { format, content, contentHash, warnings }; pass contentHash as plc_write expectedContentHash. A result larger than the budget is omitted whole with guidance: narrow it or re-run that operationId in its own plc_read call. compare_to_online, compare_hardware_to_online, get_station_fingerprint_data, scan_accessible_devices, get_umc_server_user and check_umc_consistency contact a device or server but change nothing (every mode); TLS is trusted only for SHA-256 fingerprints the user checked and approved (trustedCertificates), passwords only as password sources, never values. Reads change nothing and are no safety acceptance evidence; check_activation_test is classified as a write capability (read-only refuses it). Many operations are not live-tested. Operations: get_block_content, get_type_content, list_tag_tables, list_download_targets, read_address_occupancy, find_free_address, compare_to_online, compare_software, compare_hardware, compare_hardware_to_online, get_online_state, list_station_upload_interfaces, list_watch_and_force_tables, read_watch_table, read_force_table, get_watch_table_content, get_force_table_content, get_block_interface, get_type_interface, get_db_values, get_call_tree, find_call_paths, find_unused_blocks, find_orphaned_instance_dbs, analyze_change_impact, list_text_lists, read_text_list_workbook, read_alarm_text_workbook, read_supervision_workbook, get_prodiag_fb, get_prodiag_assignment, list_technology_objects, get_technology_object_parameters, get_technology_object_hardware_connection, get_technology_object_content, get_plc_security, list_external_sources, read_tag_comments, scan_accessible_devices, find_objects, get_db_snapshot, list_networks, get_plc_checksums, get_fingerprints, get_opcua_configuration, get_cpu_settings, get_umac, get_umc_server_user, check_umc_consistency, get_markings, get_mark_state, get_object_identifier, find_object_by_identifier, get_creation_infos, get_linked_tags, get_cpu_certificates, get_safety_validation, check_activation_test, get_block_protection, get_project_languages, get_safety_administration, list_safety_blocks, describe_operations.";

    internal const string Write = "Execute up to 50 ordered PLC software writes against one verified already-open project. Omitted dryRun or dryRun:false executes; use dryRun:true to preview effects, dependsOn and guards without mutation. Each item is { operationId, operation, ...fields } and takes only its operation's fields: get them first with plc_read describe_operations (operationNames), which returns each operation's required and optional fields, field rules, guards and verification. Content updates pass content plus expectedContentHash from a plc_read in the same format. Planning checks every item before the first one runs (a planning refusal rejects the whole call). Phases: preview, applied, blocked, error. Stops on first failure, with no rollback or automatic replay; inspect with plc_read before retrying. Every write is verified by a read-back where one exists, otherwise trusted; a failed item is never verified. plc_write never compiles or saves the project (compile_check, save_project); downloads to a controller stay with plc_download. Confirmation: no prompt unless an acknowledge guard fires; then read-write asks the human once for the call and full satisfies it by policy. Acknowledge guards: plc_safety_acceptance_required (every fail-safe item: F-blocks, F-tags, safety administration, safety validation; this server never replaces the safety acceptance by a qualified person), plc_master_secret_online and plc_loads_actual_values_online (OnlineControl on a PLC that is online: set_plc_master_secret_online, reset_plc_master_secret_online, load_snapshot_as_actual_values, load_start_values_as_actual_values), plc_syslog_auto_accepts_certificates (set_syslog with SysLogAutoAcceptClient=true), plc_protects_project (protect_project). Block guards: plc_ob_singleton_exists, plc_safety_login_required (a fail-safe change while a safety password is set and the session is not logged on; safety_login first). Info guards (deleted contents, interface changes, re-imports, lowered CPU protection, overwritten files, V21 pitfalls) are reported and do not stop the call; TIA Portal decides. Passwords only as password sources (environment variable NAME or { credential: \"TiaMcp/...\" }, or the server password map), never values. File paths are absolute drive or UNC share paths; an existing target needs overwrite:true. TIA Portal dialogs are answered by portalConfirmations (decline by default). Many operations are not live-tested. Operations: update_block_logic, update_type_content, create_tag_table, delete_tag_table, create_tag, update_tag, delete_tag, move_tag, create_user_constant, update_user_constant, delete_user_constant, create_block, delete_block, create_block_group, delete_block_group, create_watch_table, delete_watch_table, create_watch_table_group, delete_watch_table_group, update_watch_table_content, update_force_table_content, update_program, add_interface_member, update_interface_member, delete_interface_member, update_db_member, create_instance_db, rename_block, renumber_block, copy_block, move_block, move_tag_table, update_text_list, delete_text_list, update_text_list_cells, update_alarm_text_cells, update_supervision_cells, export_text_lists, import_text_lists, export_alarm_texts, import_alarm_texts, export_alarm_classes, import_alarm_classes, export_system_diagnostics_settings, import_system_diagnostics_settings, export_supervisions, import_supervisions, import_supervision_settings, set_prodiag_assignment, export_prodiag_info, create_technology_object, delete_technology_object, rename_technology_object, create_technology_object_group, delete_technology_object_group, rename_technology_object_group, set_technology_object_parameter, connect_technology_object_hardware, disconnect_technology_object_hardware, export_technology_object, import_technology_object, update_technology_object_content, set_plc_access_level, disable_plc_confidential_data_protection, protect_plc_confidential_data, change_plc_confidential_data_password, import_external_source, generate_blocks_from_source, delete_external_source, export_source_file, rename_block_group, rename_type_group, rename_tag_table_group, rename_watch_table_group, create_type_group, delete_type_group, create_tag_table_group, delete_tag_table_group, create_software_unit, delete_software_unit, rename_software_unit, export_tag_tables_csv, export_watch_tables_csv, export_force_tables_csv, export_blocks, create_db_snapshot, set_network_text, replace_network_text, rename_tags, rename_objects, replace_tag_comments, rename_members, export_tag_table, import_tag_table, export_opcua_xml, insert_network, replace_network, delete_network, create_block_from_document, set_project_compilation_settings, generate_loadable, create_opcua_interface, delete_opcua_interface, export_opcua_interface, import_opcua_interface, set_opcua_interface, set_opcua_namespace_restriction, create_opcua_role, add_opcua_standard_role, delete_opcua_role, set_opcua_role, set_opcua_namespace_permission, download_to_folder, set_plc_master_secret_online, reset_plc_master_secret_online, load_snapshot_as_actual_values, load_start_values_as_actual_values, set_account_locking, set_plc_password_policy, set_legacy_plc_password_policy, set_syslog, add_syslog_server, remove_syslog_server, create_project_syslog_server, update_project_syslog_server, delete_project_syslog_server, set_system_web_pages, set_default_web_application, set_watch_table_access, remove_watch_table_access, set_force_table_access, remove_force_table_access, set_display_password, set_front_panel_display, set_plc_project_language, set_ip_accessibility, generate_web_blocks, create_webserver_user, update_webserver_user, delete_webserver_user, update_simple_webserver_user, create_opcua_user, set_opcua_user_password, delete_opcua_user, create_custom_role, update_custom_role, delete_custom_role, assign_engineering_right, unassign_engineering_right, assign_device_function_right, unassign_device_function_right, create_project_user, update_project_user, delete_project_user, assign_user_role, unassign_user_role, set_anonymous_user, create_custom_device_function_right, update_custom_device_function_right, delete_custom_device_function_right, update_umc_user, delete_umc_user, set_umac_password_policy, protect_project, create_offline_umc_user, create_offline_umc_user_group, import_umc_user, mark_objects, unmark_objects, save_cam_data, load_cam_data, set_certificate_manager, create_cpu_certificate, import_cpu_certificate, export_cpu_certificate, delete_cpu_certificate, assign_cpu_certificate, unassign_cpu_certificate, set_certificate_management, add_certificate_supported_service, update_certificate_supported_service, remove_certificate_supported_service, generate_safety_printout, create_activation_test, delete_activation_test, change_activation_test_evaluation_device, create_activation_test_group, delete_activation_test_group, create_safety_function, update_safety_function, delete_safety_function, reset_safety_function_test_result, create_safety_function_condition, update_safety_function_condition, delete_safety_function_condition, export_activation_test, generate_activation_test_report, set_block_know_how_protection, remove_block_know_how_protection, define_block_write_protection, set_block_write_protection, remove_block_write_protection, change_block_write_protection_password, set_project_languages, export_project_texts, import_project_texts, safety_login, safety_logoff, set_safety_password, revoke_safety_password, create_safety_runtime_group, set_safety_runtime_group.";

    internal const string ReadOperationsParameter = "Ordered list of PLC read operations. Each item is { operationId, operation, ...operation parameters }. Item field descriptions are abbreviated; describe_operations returns the full rules.";

    internal const string WriteOperationsParameter = "Ordered PLC write operations. Item field descriptions are abbreviated; plc_read describe_operations returns each operation's fields and full rules.";
}

/// <summary>
/// The full plc_read and plc_write reference texts, as the tool descriptions carried them before K91. Kept here verbatim
/// (an operation named in a group is spelled out so every operation is found) and served by describe_operations.
/// </summary>
internal static partial class PlcOperationReference
{
    internal const string ReadTool = "Run up to 50 PLC read operations in one call. Valid operations: get_block_content (blockPath, optional format xml|source|sd and withDependencies; sd returns only the SIMATIC SD documents of PlcBlock.ExportAsDocuments (.s7dcl, and .s7res when exported) delimited like the xml bundle, with an sd:sha256 contentHash and failSafe true when the .s7dcl header declares S7_Safety := \"TRUE\"; whatever TIA Portal refuses to export fails with its error; xml returns the SimaticML .xml plus the SD documents, and when TIA Portal exports no SimaticML (it does not export inconsistent blocks, e.g. one not compiled since it was created; confirmed live on V21 2026-11-02) the result holds the SD documents only and a warning says so: run compile_check and read again; live-tested on V21 2026-11-02: a block without texts exports only the .s7dcl), list_networks (blockPath; from the sd export: blockKind, blockName, preferredLanguage, failSafe, every header pragma (S7_PreferredLanguage, S7_Safety, ...), and per network its 1-based number in document order, language (S7_Language pragma, else detected from the RUNG syntax as the Siemens V21 simatic-sd skill does: languageSource pragma|detected, null when ambiguous), every pragma entry, titleId/title and commentId/comment resolved from the .s7res (S7_NetworkTitle, S7_NetworkComment ids, one text per culture), the body (code, common indentation removed) and exportOnlyForms (instruction forms the V21 export writes that are reported not to re-import; not reproduced live 2026-11-02 for GT/EQ_Contact, Move, P_Trig/N_Trig, TON/TOF, Add); contentHash is the sd hash for insert_network, replace_network and delete_network; live-tested on V21 2026-11-02), get_type_content (typePath, optional format and withDependencies), list_tag_tables (optional plcName, omitted reads every PLC; optional tableName and folderPath narrow to one table or one tag-table folder), list_download_targets (optional plcName, omitted reads every PLC; the offline download path for plc_download: connection modes, PC interfaces { name, number } and target interfaces, read from the project without going online or scanning the network), get_plc_security (optional plcName, omitted reads every PLC; CPU protection per CPU for diagnosing download and hardware compile errors: accessLevel (PlcAccessLevelProvider.PlcProtectionAccessLevel; readable false with a note when no password is configured, as Siemens documents), accessControl (PlcAccessControlConfigurationProvider.Configuration), confidentialDataProtection (PlcMasterSecretConfigurator: protectBindable, unprotectBindable, unprotectCandidates and the service's readable properties uninterpreted, because no documented member reports the checkbox state) and the CPU's service type names; every member is bound at runtime, not live-tested; never reads or handles a password), read_address_occupancy (assignment list of one PLC: declared I/Q/M tags plus, unless includeHardware is false, the PLC's hardware I/O addresses; optional plcName, areas; a tag's width is its data type's documented length, cross-checked with the address spelling; reports tag overlaps, I/Q tags outside hardware ranges, widthMismatches, tags without an absolute address and unsizedTags whose data type has no documented length, which make isComplete false), find_free_address (area I|Q|M and dataType; optional plcName, startByte and endByte 0..65535, alignBytes, requireHardware; the lowest address not used by any declared tag; isComplete is false when the inventory is incomplete or an unsized tag lies in the area), get_online_state (optional plcName; OnlineProvider.State, IsConfigured and the offline online path for plc_tia_online), list_station_upload_interfaces (the offline modes and PC interfaces for plc_station_upload), compare_software (compareTarget plc|project_library|master_copy|secondary_plc, targetName for plc, master_copy and secondary_plc, targetProject for secondary_plc (the path of an open secondary project, library_write open_secondary_project; issue #20, not live-tested), optional plcName, maxDepth, maxElements, differencesOnly; PlcSoftware.CompareTo, offline), compare_to_online (optional plcName, maxDepth, maxElements, differencesOnly, trustedCertificates, passwords { OnlineReadAccessPassword: source, ... } (password sources, never values; omitted entries come from the server password map); PlcSoftware.CompareToOnline: connects to the PLC with the path TIA Portal has configured but changes nothing; a connection the compare opened is closed again; allowed in every mode), compare_hardware and compare_hardware_to_online (issue #7, not live-tested; HardwareObject.CompareTo(IHardwareCompareTarget) of the PLC's station (hardwareScope device, default) or CPU device item (cpu): compare_hardware takes compareTarget plc (the other PLC's object of the same scope, targetName) or master_copy (a root master copy of the project library, targetName), compare_hardware_to_online the CPU's OnlineProvider as the target with optional trustedCertificates and passwords under exactly the rules of compare_to_online (connection closed again, TLS trusted only from trustedCertificates, allowed in every mode); V21 does not document which types implement IHardwareCompareTarget, so a target that does not implement it at runtime is unsupported_capability before anything is compared or contacted; same bounded tree and caps), get_station_fingerprint_data (audit N3, not live-tested: mode, pcInterface { name, number } and targetAddress required, optional maxElements (default 200, at most 2000), trustedCertificates, passwords and onlineUser; FingerprintDataProvider.GetFingerprintData(ConfigurationAddress, OnlineConfigurationDelegate) of the station at that node address for a quick station compare, the provider found among the GetServiceInfos() of TIA Portal, then of the bound project, the address created on the PC interface of the provider's own Configuration; online prompts are answered under the compare_to_online rules and every TIA Portal dialog is answered No; it contacts the device but changes nothing, allowed in every mode; returns every FingerprintDataItem's identifier and value as text { state, value, runtimeType, error }), list_watch_and_force_tables (optional plcName), read_watch_table and read_force_table (tableName, optional plcName, folderPath group path and maxElements; entries read attribute by attribute), get_watch_table_content and get_force_table_content (tableName, optional plcName and folderPath; SimaticML with contentHash for update_watch_table_content/update_force_table_content), get_block_interface (blockPath: block identity with number, language and know-how protection, the xml contentHash and the interface sections as a member tree with data types, start values, comments and exported attributes), get_type_interface (typePath: the same for a PLC data type) and get_db_values (blockPath of a global or instance DB, optional memberPath to narrow and withAttributes: start values per value path, read with Interface.Members.Find, expanding structs, PLC data types, multi-instances and arrays up to 400 values), get_db_snapshot (blockPath of a global or instance DB, optional memberPath and maxElements 1-20000 default 2000: the snapshot of actual values stored in the offline project, InterfaceSnapshot.Export with ExportOptions.WithReadOnly, as { snapshotDate, values [{ path, value, dataType }] }; hasSnapshot false when none is stored; take one with plc_write create_db_snapshot; members bound at runtime, a missing one fails api_member_missing; not live-tested). Program analysis, computed from the block inventory and the read_cross_references reader (one sweep per root block folder of the PLC, shared by every analysis item of the call): get_call_tree (blockPath of an OB/FB/FC; optional maxDepth, maxElements, timeoutSeconds; forward call and multi-instance relations with instance DBs per node, cycles and repeats marked), find_call_paths (blockPath; every path from an OB to the block, bounded), find_unused_blocks (optional plcName; blocks no OB reaches, with categories), find_orphaned_instance_dbs (optional plcName; reads each instance DB's SimaticML InstanceOfName and reports DBs whose FB is not in the inventory or not reached) and analyze_change_impact (exactly one of blockPath, typePath, or tableName with name for a tag; direct and transitive users). A relationship is used only when a cross-reference location states it: referenceType UsedBy or Uses gives the direction, access Call/UC/CC a call, Multiinstance a multi-instance; anything else is reported as undirected evidence, never guessed. Each analysis result carries complete, truncation and evidence { crossReferenceQueries, rules, limits }; indirect calls (block parameters, ANY/VARIANT/DB_ANY pointers, runtime DB numbers) are invisible, so an unreachable block is a candidate, not proof. Not live-tested. External sources, folders and devices (not live-tested): list_external_sources (optional plcName; the external sources of each PLC and of its software units, by name; groups inside the External source files folder are not supported by Openness and not listed), read_tag_comments (optional plcName, tableName, folderPath; the multilingual comment of every tag and user constant, one {culture, text} entry per language with a text), find_objects (pattern with * and ?, matched case-insensitively against the whole name; optional plcName, kinds, offset, limit 1-1000; software units, blocks, block groups, PLC data types and their groups, tag tables and their folders, tags and user constants of the PLC's own tag tables, watch tables, force tables and their groups, external sources, from the project tree, list_tag_tables, list_watch_and_force_tables and list_external_sources; sorted, paged, with totalMatches, nextOffset and complete; technology objects are not searched) and scan_accessible_devices (mode and pcInterface { name, number } as get_online_state lists them, both required, no default; optional plcName and maxElements 1-1000; ConfigurationPcInterface.GetAccessibleDevices() performs live network discovery through that one interface and changes nothing, allowed in every mode like compare_to_online (the access mode is the only control; the caller names the interface); TIA Portal dialogs during the scan are answered No and fail the item; each device reports name, deviceSeries, address and macAddress). Alarms and text lists (not live-tested): list_text_lists (optional plcName, omitted reads every PLC; projectLanguages { active, editing, reference } and per PLC the user and system text lists with name, isSystem, id, listRange and comment per culture; text list entries are not part of the documented object model), read_text_list_workbook (optional plcName, textListNames, cultures, maxElements, sheet, startRow, startColumn), read_alarm_text_workbook (exportOption, a PlcAlarmTextXlsxExportOption member; optional plcName, cultures, maxElements, sheet, startRow, startColumn) and read_supervision_workbook (blockPath of a ProDiag FB, optional maxElements, sheet, startRow, startColumn): TIA Portal's XLSX export into a temporary file that is deleted again (every TIA Portal dialog during it is answered No and fails the read), returned as uninterpreted cells { sheets[{ name, rowCount, columnCount, cellCount, rows[{ row, cells[{ cell, kind, value, valueTruncated }], cellsTruncated, nextStartColumn }], rowsTruncated, nextStartRow }], workbookHash } (the column layout is TIA Portal's; at most maxElements rows per sheet, default 50, and never more than the value budget, which several workbook reads of one call share: page on with sheet and startRow = nextStartRow, and a row cut at the budget with startRow = that row and startColumn = nextStartColumn; workbookHash covers every cell and is the expectedWorkbookHash of plc_write update_*_cells). get_prodiag_fb (blockPath: ProgrammingLanguage, isProDiag, FB.Supervisions.Count, IsConsistent and the ProDiagVersion, InitialValueAcquisition, UseCentralTimeStamp attributes) and get_prodiag_assignment (AssignedProDiagFB of a tag: tableName and name, optional folderPath and plcName; or of an instance DB or global DB member: blockPath, optional memberPath). Technology objects (PlcSoftware.TechnologicalObjectGroup; not live-tested): list_technology_objects (optional plcName; optional folderPath narrows one PLC to a group subtree; objects with name, groupPath, number, systemLibElement and systemLibVersion (OfSystemLibElement/OfSystemLibVersion), runtimeType, and the user groups), get_technology_object_parameters (name; optional prefix, offset and limit 1-2000 default 200 with nextOffset, or parameterName for one exact Find; every value is typed by its runtime type: valueKind boolean|integer|real|string|enum|plcTag|null|object|unreadable, valueType, value as invariant text and enumMembers), get_technology_object_hardware_connection (name; every documented provider the object lists among its services: actor, sensor and torque (axis), sensor (encoder), measuringInput, outputCam, ident, with isConnected and the documented properties, connected modules as modulePath) and get_technology_object_content (name; SimaticML with contentHash for update_technology_object_content). Fail-safe (F-) PLCs (not live-tested; every Siemens.Engineering.Safety member is bound at runtime by exact name, a missing one is reported api_member_missing): get_safety_administration (optional plcName, omitted reads every PLC; per PLC whether its CPU offers SafetyAdministration, passwordSet (IsSafetyOfflineProgramPasswordSet), loggedOn (IsLoggedOnToSafetyOfflineProgram), the SafetySettings values (SafetySystemVersion, applicable versions, F-change history, block number ranges), every F-runtime group with its attributes (main safety block and IDB, F-OB, cycle times) and attributeInfos (every attribute GetAttributeInfos lists, with its access mode, to see what is writable), the collective program signatures, the Safety services the CPU lists and the safety unit names; plus TIA Portal's GlobalSettings getters such as SafetyModificationsPossible) and list_safety_blocks (optional plcName, offset, limit 1-2000 default 200; every block that offers SafetySignatureProvider or has an F_ language, with its signatures). Reads change nothing and are no safety acceptance evidence. Offline change detection (issue #6; not live-tested; every member is bound at runtime): get_plc_checksums (optional plcName, omitted reads every PLC; per PLC whether its PlcSoftware lists and returns Siemens.Engineering.SW.PlcChecksumProvider among GetServiceInfos(), and its Software and TextLists checksums projected as text { state value|empty|null|unreadable|missing, value, runtimeType, error } because the reference gives no type; empty or null means, per the Siemens change-detection skill, not compiled or changed since the last compile) and get_fingerprints (exactly one of blockPath or typePath; FingerprintProvider.GetFingerprints() of that block or PLC data type, found among its GetServiceInfos() (not listed: unsupported_capability; GetFingerprints missing: api_member_missing), every Fingerprint's Id and Value as text in the same shape). The online FingerprintDataProvider is not offered. Project languages (issue #8, not live-tested): get_project_languages (no fields; project-wide: LanguageSettings.ActiveLanguages, EditingLanguage and ReferenceLanguage as culture names, every supported language of LanguageSettings.Languages, and the text categories { identifier, name } of ProjectBase.TextCategories that export_project_texts takes). Block protection (issue #5, not live-tested): get_block_protection (blockPath; the block's PlcBlock.IsKnowHowProtected, programming language and isFailSafe, and for PlcBlockProtectionProvider (know-how) and PlcBlockWriteProtectionProvider (IsDefined, IsProtected) whether the block's GetServiceInfos() lists and returns them, which documented members bind and the characters GetInvalidPasswordCharacters() returns; an unreadable value is null with a note). OPC UA (issue #24; not live-tested; members bound at runtime): get_opcua_configuration (optional plcName, omitted reads every PLC; from the PlcSoftware's OpcUaProvider service (not listed: providerAvailable false with a note): the server interfaces (companion specifications and own interfaces), SIMATIC interfaces and reference namespaces with name, enabled, author, comment, creationTime, lastModified, useStringNodeIds, generateNodes, generatedInterfaceName, and the access control: namespace access restrictions (namespaceUri, namespaceIndex, sessionRequired, signingRequired, encryptionRequired, applyRestrictionsToBrowse) and role mappings (name, definedInNamespace, projectRole, roleId, namespacePermissions with browse, read, write, call, receiveEvents, readRolePermissions)). Reads run independently, so a failing item does not stop later operations. Content results are { format, content, contentHash, warnings }; contentHash is null for withDependencies reads. list_tag_tables returns { isComplete, messages, plcs[] } and list_download_targets returns { plcs[{ plcName, deviceName, downloadable, modes[] }] } as declared JSON; compare results are a bounded { root { leftName, rightName, comparisonResult, detailedInformation, elements[] } } tree with identical, complete and omission. A result larger than the budget is omitted whole with guidance; narrow it or re-run that operationId in its own plc_read call. get_cpu_settings (optional plcName; issue #15, not live-tested): per CPU the account locking, syslog (with its servers and the syslog attributes), system web pages, web applications, watch/force table access rules of the web server and the display, display protection, front panel display, user-defined web pages, the MultilingualSupport rows and the IP accessibility module, plus the project's PLC password policies and syslog servers; values are projected as text, uninterpreted, and a service the CPU does not offer is reported as not offered. get_cpu_settings also lists the CPU's web server users (with permissions), simple web server users and the OPC UA submodule's users (issue #13; passwords are never readable). Engineering objects by objectPath (package G, not live-tested; the grammar of plc_write's objectPath): get_markings (the bound Multiuser local session's MarkingService.GetMarkings: AllMarkings and ConflictedMarkings with object and MarkState), get_mark_state (objectPath; GetMarkStateInfo and IsMarkable), get_object_identifier (objectPath; ObjectIdentifierProvider.GetIdentifier), find_object_by_identifier (name = identifier; ObjectIdentifierProvider.Find), get_creation_infos (objectPath, optional name of one composition; IEngineeringObject.GetCompositionInfos and GetCreationInfos: what can be created in each composition, with each parameter, whether it is mandatory and its supported types; with name also IEngineeringComposition.GetCreationInfos of that composition), get_linked_tags (objectPath channel:...; the channel's PlcTagProvider.GetLinkedTags: Name, LogicalAddress, DataTypeName, TagTable); get_umc_server_user (name, optional userKind umcUser|umcUserGroup, optional UMC server credentials userName + passwordVariable; UmcServer.GetUserByName/GetUserGroupByName: Found, Name or UserGroupName and Description) and check_umc_consistency (optional credentials; UmcServerConfigurator.CheckConsistency(): Consistent) contact the UMC server and change nothing (OnlineObserve, every mode; package G, not live-tested); get_umac (optional plcName; issue #12, not live-tested): the project's UMAC (engineering function rights, which make the project protected when not empty, custom and system roles with their engineering rights, project users with alias, state, session timeout, authentication type and roles, UMC users and groups, custom device function rights, the anonymous user, the password policy) and per PLC the UmacDevice's available device function rights and every role's assigned rights on it. get_cpu_certificates (optional plcName; issue #14, not live-tested; TemporaryExport): per CPU the LocalCertificateManager (EnableGlobalCertificatesStore) with every certificate of its LocalCertificateStore (Id, SubjectCommonName, ValidUntil, HasPrivateKey and, from a temporary Export(FileInfo) deleted afterwards, Sha256 over the DER bytes, Sha1Thumbprint, Subject, Issuer, NotBefore, NotAfter), the dynamic certificate management (Usage, CertificateExpirationEventActivated, RemainingCertificateLifetime, CertificateSupportedServices) and the certificates assigned through WebserverCertificate and OpcUaServerCertificate. Compare these SHA-256 fingerprints with the ones a TLS prompt lists before passing trustedCertificates; nothing here trusts a certificate. get_safety_validation (issue #25, not live-tested): the Safety Validation Assistant's activation tests with group, author, evaluation device and overall state, their safety functions (test name, description, test state, traced) and conditions, the groups and the evaluation devices. check_activation_test (testName, optional functionName, position): TestValidity.CheckValidity() of the test, function or condition (state, error count, messages); a consistency check, no test result and no acceptance. Whether CheckValidity stores a validity state is undocumented, so it is classified as a write capability: read-only refuses it.";

    internal const string WriteTool = "Execute up to 50 ordered PLC software writes against one verified already-open project. Omitted dryRun or dryRun:false executes; use dryRun:true to preview effects, dependsOn and guards without mutation. No confirmation prompt is sent unless an acknowledge guard fires (then read-write asks the human once for the call and full satisfies it by policy). Operations: update_block_logic (blockPath, content, expectedContentHash, optional format xml (default) | source | sd; sd imports the bundle of get_block_content sd with PlcBlockComposition.ImportFromDocuments(..., ImportDocumentOptions.Override): exactly one .s7dcl declaring the target block, optionally its .s7res, no .xml; a bundle without .xml in format xml still takes that route as before), update_type_content (typePath, content, expectedContentHash), create_tag_table/delete_tag_table (tableName), create_tag/update_tag/delete_tag (create_tag and update_tag take an optional comment with commentCulture: the PlcTag.Comment text item of that culture (LanguageSettings.Languages, Comment.Items.Find) gets the text, read back; a culture that is no active project language is passed on with a warning and TIA Portal decides, one it has no text item for fails (create_tag then deletes the tag it created, update_tag keeps its other changes), one TIA Portal does not know is refused before anything changes; create_tag, delete_tag and a commented update_tag are verified by re-reading the tag table and the comment, check tag), move_tag (tableName, name, targetTableName, optional folderPath and targetFolderPath; re-created in the target table with its data type, address, external-access flags and multilingual comment in one transaction that a failure rolls back; other attributes are not carried; verified by re-reading both tables, check tag), create_user_constant/update_user_constant/delete_user_constant (tableName, name), create_block (blockPath, blockType, language, obEventClass for OB; the worker re-resolves the created block by its path, which is the verification, check block; it is not compiled), delete_block (verified by re-reading the path: it must be gone, check block; a later item that creates the same block name in any group supersedes it, block names being unique per PLC), create_block_group, delete_block_group (blockPath), create_watch_table/delete_watch_table (tableName, optional folderPath group path), create_watch_table_group/delete_watch_table_group (folderPath names the group), update_watch_table_content/update_force_table_content (tableName, content, expectedContentHash from get_watch_table_content/get_force_table_content; entries are added, changed and removed only through this SimaticML round trip, and force tables are edited offline only, never forced online), update_program (optional plcName; PlcSoftware.UpdateProgram upgrades block instructions to the latest version the PLC firmware supports, offline); granular block edits: add_interface_member (blockPath+section or typePath, memberPath, dataType, optional startValue, comment+commentCulture, insertBefore), update_interface_member (newName, dataType, startValue, clearStartValue, comment), delete_interface_member — a SimaticML edit of the exported document imported through update_block_logic/update_type_content with the export's hash and verified by re-reading the member; optional expectedContentHash (xml); update_db_member (blockPath, memberPath at any depth incl. array elements and multi-instances, startValue and/or externalAccessible, externalVisible, externalWritable, retain, setPoint; native Member.SetAttribute, read back); create_db_snapshot (blockPath of a global or instance DB, optional memberPath and maxElements for the returned values; the PLC must be online (plc_tia_online go_online): ValueService.CreateSnapshot() takes the actual values, TIA Portal stores them as the DB's snapshot in the offline project (info guard plc_stores_db_snapshot; nothing is written to the PLC, no start value changes), and the result is the exported snapshot, verified by re-reading it (check dbSnapshot); adopted from BetterTIA/watch watch_db, members bound at runtime, not live-tested); set_network_text (blockPath of an OB, FB or FC, networkNumber 1-based, title and/or comment, optional culture, expectedContentHash xml; a language the network has no text in yet is added) and replace_network_text (blockPath, replacements [{ find, replace }] 1-100 applied in one pass, literal and case-sensitive, longest find first so swaps work; optional culture (omitted: every language) and textScope networks (default) | all (also the block title/comment and the GRAPH sequence, step and transition texts)): Openness has no setter for network texts, so the exported SimaticML is edited host-side and imported through update_block_logic against the export's hash (know-how-protected blocks refused; an edit that changes nothing is refused before anything runs; info guard plc_text_edit_reimports_block: the import can leave the instance DB and callers inconsistent, compile afterwards); verified by re-export (check networkText: every changed text reads back at its place and language, contentHash reported); adopted from BetterTIA/writer, not live-tested; rename_members (blockPath or typePath, memberRenames [{ memberPath, newName, section? }] 1-100, optional expectedContentHash xml): renames several interface members together (swaps and rotations through temporary names) and updates the object's own accesses as the TIA Portal editor does (LocalVariable symbols and instances in LAD/FBD/STL/SCL/GRAPH networks, #operands in GRAPH actions); accesses in other blocks, HMI tags, watch tables and technology objects are not updated (info guard plc_changes_interface; read analyze_change_impact first and compile afterwards); instance and array DBs refused; verified by re-reading the interface (check renamedMembers); adopted from BetterTIA/writer RenameMembers, not live-tested; rename_tags (optional plcName, renames [{ name, newName }] 1-200: PLC tags by name across every tag table of the PLC) and rename_objects (optional plcName, renames: blocks, PLC data types and technology objects by name, a name in more than one kind is ambiguous): every object resolved before anything changes, then SetAttribute(\"Name\") per step (GetAttributeInfos writability check and read-back) in one ExclusiveAccess transaction, with swaps, rotations and chains through temporary names (zzTmp_...); any failed step rolls every rename back and the failure reports the names afterwards; fail-safe tags and F-blocks follow TIA Portal's safety login rule (info guard plc_batch_rename; users re-bind by name at the next compile, HMI tags and watch tables are not changed); verified by re-reading the tag tables (rename_tags) or by the transaction's read-back (rename_objects), check batchRename; adopted from BetterTIA/writer, not live-tested; replace_tag_comments (optional plcName, tableName with folderPath for one table, replacements [{ find, replace }] 1-100 in one pass as replace_network_text, optional culture): every PLC tag comment text in scope that a find changes is set through MultilingualTextItem.Text and read back in one ExclusiveAccess transaction (rollback on failure); the preview lists every changed text from read_tag_comments, an item that changes nothing is refused; verified by re-reading the comments (check tagComments); tags of the PLC's own tag tables only; it changes existing texts only, so give a tag without a comment its first text with update_tag comment+commentCulture; adopted from BetterTIA/writer, not live-tested; SIMATIC SD network edits (the path the Siemens V21 simatic-sd skill names for adding LAD/FBD/SCL networks to existing blocks; not live-tested): insert_network (blockPath, code, optional language, position 1-based (omitted appends), expectedContentHash sd), replace_network (blockPath, networkNumber, code, optional language (omitted keeps the network's), expectedContentHash sd; the network's pragma keys such as S7_NetworkTitle/S7_NetworkComment stay) and delete_network (blockPath, networkNumber, expectedContentHash sd; the network and its pragma are removed): planned host-side on the get_block_content sd export (code: a RUNG body, a full NETWORK ... END_NETWORK with or without its pragma, or SCL statements; only the outer wrappers and the S7_Language pragma are stripped, inner { S7_Templates := \"...\" } pragmas stay; one network per code; unbalanced RUNG/END_RUNG or NETWORK/END_NETWORK and S7_NetworkTitle/S7_NetworkComment keys are refused, everything else is TIA Portal's to accept), imported through update_block_logic format sd against the export's hash; the .s7res is never changed; several items on one block chain through dependsOn and are re-planned (a later item numbers the networks as the earlier ones left them); info guards plc_text_edit_reimports_block (compile afterwards), plc_sd_reimports_export_form (untouched networks in an export form reported not to re-import; not reproduced live on V21 for GT/EQ_Contact, Move, P_Trig/N_Trig, TON/TOF, Add) and plc_s7dcl_import_may_alter; verified by re-export (check networkCode: network count, position and language must match; the message reports codeMatchesExport true|false with both texts in expected/actual, as information, because the V21 export form of an instruction is reported to differ from its import form and TIA Portal reformats whitespace; contentHash sd reported). create_block_from_document (targetGroupPath, content: an sd bundle with the .s7dcl and, optionally, the .s7res (TIA Portal's own export of a block without texts has none); every culture in the .s7res must be a project language (a culture the project lacks failed the import live; the item reports the cultures it holds), optional overwrite): ImportFromDocuments into that group; a block of the declared name anywhere in the PLC is refused unless overwrite:true (info guard plc_sd_document_replaces_block); verified by re-exporting it in sd (check createdBlock, contentHash sd). A header S7_Safety := \"TRUE\" marks a fail-safe block for every SD write (the safety rules below apply). create_instance_db (blockPath, instanceOfName, optional number); rename_block (newName); renumber_block (number or autoNumber:true); copy_block (newName, optional targetGroupPath, number) and move_block (targetGroupPath) by SimaticML export/import, refusing know-how-protected blocks (their export carries only the interface); move_tag_table (tableName, folderPath, targetFolderPath) by export/delete/import with re-import on failure. OPC UA export (not live-tested; idea from heilingbrunner/tiaportal-mcp, MIT): export_opcua_xml (filePath, optional plcName and overwrite) writes the OPC UA data of the PLC's CPU as XML through Project.HwUtilities.Find(\"OPCUAExportProvider\") and OpcUaExportProvider.Export(DeviceItem, FileInfo), bound at runtime (api_member_missing when absent); staged, moved into place and re-hashed like export_tag_table, an existing file needs overwrite:true (info guard plc_export_overwrites_file); TIA Portal is reported to need the PLC offline. Tag tables as SimaticML files (not live-tested): export_tag_table (tableName, optional folderPath, filePath, overwrite; PlcTagTable.Export(FileInfo, ExportOptions.None) into a temporary file, staged next to the target, moved into place and re-hashed; an existing file needs overwrite:true, info guard plc_export_overwrites_file) and import_tag_table (filePath, optional folderPath, tableName and overwrite; PlcTagTableComposition.Import(FileInfo, ImportOptions) bound at runtime, of a private copy of the file, in one ExclusiveAccess transaction that a failed postcondition rolls back; overwrite:true imports with ImportOptions.Override (info guard plc_import_replaces_tag_table); tableName names the table the file holds and is then checked: it must not exist without overwrite and must be in the folder afterwards; verified by re-reading the tag tables, check tagTable); the CSV export export_tag_tables_csv stays. External sources (not live-tested): import_external_source (absolute local filePath of a .scl, .awl, .db or .udt file, optional sourceName defaulting to the file name, plcName, unitName; PlcExternalSourceComposition.CreateFromFile), generate_blocks_from_source (sourceName, optional generateOption None|KeepOnError and targetGroupPath block or PLC data type group; creates or overwrites every block and PLC data type the source declares), delete_external_source (sourceName; generated blocks stay), export_source_file (filePath, blockPaths and/or typePaths of one PLC scope, optional withDependencies and overwrite; GenerateSource into a temporary file next to the target, then moved into place). Group renames (not live-tested): rename_block_group (blockPath of the group), rename_type_group (typePath of the group), rename_tag_table_group (folderPath, optional unitName) and rename_watch_table_group (folderPath), each with newName, through SetAttribute(\"Name\") after a GetAttributeInfos writability check, read back. Group and software unit containers (not live-tested): create_type_group and delete_type_group (typePath of the group, e.g. PLC_1/Types/Motion or PLC_1/Units/U1/Types/Motion), create_tag_table_group and delete_tag_table_group (folderPath, optional plcName, unitName); the parent of a create must exist; deleting a group that is not empty removes everything inside it (info guard plc_deletes_group_contents). create_software_unit, delete_software_unit (unitName, optional plcName; a delete removes the unit's blocks, types, tag tables and external sources, info guard plc_deletes_group_contents) and rename_software_unit (unitName, newName; SetAttribute(\"Name\") with writability check and read-back). Each create is read back with Find(name), each delete must be gone afterwards. File exports from existing reads (not live-tested): export_tag_tables_csv, export_watch_tables_csv and export_force_tables_csv (filePath ending in .csv, optional plcName, tableName, folderPath, csvDelimiter, rawCells, overwrite; the tag CSV adds one Comment[culture] column per comment language read_tag_comments returns; RFC 4180, UTF-8 with BOM, a cell starting with =, +, -, @, tab or CR gets a leading ' unless rawCells) and export_blocks (directoryPath, optional plcName, blockPath or typePath group, format xml|source, maxElements, overwrite; one file per exported document below a project-tree mirror, each with its SHA-256). Every file is written through a temporary file and moved into place; an existing file is refused unless overwrite:true; drive paths and UNC shares (\\\\server\\share\\...) are accepted, device paths (\\\\?\\, \\\\.\\) are refused. Alarms, text lists and ProDiag supervisions (not live-tested): update_text_list (textListName, optional newName, listRange, comment with commentCulture; every requested member must be writable per GetAttributeInfos and a new name must be free among the user and system lists, checked before the first change; the rename runs first and everything is read back) and delete_text_list (textListName); system text lists are refused; a user text list is created with library_write instantiate_master_copy target kind textLists; update_text_list_cells, update_alarm_text_cells and update_supervision_cells (cellEdits [{ sheet, cell, expected, value, kind? }] and expectedWorkbookHash from the matching read_*_workbook with the same plcName, blockPath, textListNames, cultures and exportOption; update_text_list_cells requires textListNames, user text lists only, and exports and imports only those lists) export the workbook, refuse a changed hash or an unexpected cell value, patch only the edited cells, import the whole workbook with TIA Portal's XLSX import and re-export it, all under ExclusiveAccess, and fail when the re-export misses an edit or changed any other cell (result.unrequestedChanges); they cannot follow another change of the same PLC in one call; export_text_lists, export_alarm_texts, export_alarm_classes and export_supervisions (filePath, optional overwrite; TIA Portal writes a temporary file in the target directory that is moved into place, and an existing file is replaced only with overwrite:true, never through a link) and import_text_lists, import_alarm_texts (optional exportOption for its verification re-export), import_alarm_classes, import_supervisions and import_supervision_settings (filePath): TIA Portal decides what an import changes; the server imports a private copy of the file (result bytes and sha256 are that copy's) and re-exports the same kind right after it: importCheck.outcome verified (every imported row, columns matched by header, or for alarm classes the whole file, came back; check importedRows or fileHash), contradicted (an imported row is absent: notVerified, verification success false), inconclusive (layouts differ, the alarm-class file differs, or the verification export failed; check trusted with a warning) or notReadBack (import_supervision_settings and import_alarm_texts without exportOption have no documented export; check trusted with a warning); the import itself has changed the project in every case. set_prodiag_assignment (proDiagFb and the target of get_prodiag_assignment; read back by FB name, a value that does not read back as a name is notVerified) and export_prodiag_info (blockPath of a ProDiag FB, directoryPath that does not exist yet; CodeBlock.ExportProDIAGInfo writes CSV files into it, each re-hashed; an export that writes no file fails postcondition_failed). Every alarm write takes portalConfirmations (decline, the default: a TIA Portal dialog is answered No and fails the item; accept: Yes, with a warning); result.portalConfirmations records each. Alarm classes are project-wide (no plcName, standalone projects only). System diagnostics settings (issue #19; project-wide, no plcName, standalone projects only; not live-tested): export_system_diagnostics_settings (filePath, optional overwrite, portalConfirmations) and import_system_diagnostics_settings (filePath, portalConfirmations) call SystemdiagnosticsSettingsDataProvider.Export(FileInfo)/Import(FileInfo), the provider found among the Project's GetServiceInfos() (not listed: unsupported_capability), with the same caller-file rules as the alarm classes (staged export, overwrite:true, re-hash; import of a private copy verified by a byte compare of a re-export); result State Success succeeds, Warning succeeds with a warning, anything else fails; no file extension is required (none is documented; TIA Portal may refuse one). OPC UA server interfaces and access rules (issue #24; not live-tested; PlcSoftware OpcUaProvider service, members bound at runtime, a missing one fails api_member_missing with nothing changed; info guard plc_opcua_changes_server, plc_opcua_lowers_access when a restriction is relaxed or a permission granted): create_opcua_interface (interfaceKind server|simatic|referenceNamespace, interfaceName; ServerInterfaceComposition/SimaticInterfaceComposition.Create(String), ReferenceNamespaceComposition.Create(String, FileInfo) with filePath (required for referenceNamespace; for a server interface an optional XML imported right after the create)), delete_opcua_interface, export_opcua_interface (filePath, overwrite; Export(FileInfo) staged and re-hashed), import_opcua_interface (server or referenceNamespace, filePath; Import(FileInfo) of a private copy, verified by a byte compare of a re-export, otherwise notVerified), set_opcua_interface (enabled, useStringNodeIds, generateNodes, newName through SetAttribute after a GetAttributeInfos writability check, read back), set_opcua_namespace_restriction (namespaceUri; sessionRequired, signingRequired, encryptionRequired, applyRestrictionsToBrowse, read back), create_opcua_role (roleName, definingNamespace; RoleMappingComposition.Create), add_opcua_standard_role (roleName; AddStandardOpcUaRole), delete_opcua_role, set_opcua_role (roleName; newRoleName, definingNamespace, projectRole via SetRoleName/SetDefiningNamespace/SetProjectRole, read back) and set_opcua_namespace_permission (roleName, namespaceUri, permission, enabled; NamespacePermission.SetPermission(String, Boolean), read back through the property of that name when it is one of Browse, Read, Write, Call, ReceiveEvents, ReadRolePermissions, otherwise notVerified); every item takes optional plcName (the only PLC when omitted). Further download variants and the PLC master secret (issue #16; not live-tested): download_to_folder (directoryPath, an existing absolute directory; optional plcName, rhSystem (true: the R/H system's RHDownloadProvider), overwrite, portalConfirmations): DownloadProvider.Download(DirectoryInfo, DownloadConfigurationDelegate) writes the download data into the folder, no device is touched; a directory that is not empty is refused unless overwrite:true, and junctions, links and network locations are checked and reported like the other directory exports; download configurations get the built-in plc_download answers, any other one aborts; verified by the files the call wrote (re-hashed). set_plc_master_secret_online (passwordVariable: an environment variable NAME or { credential: \"TiaMcp/...\" }, never the secret) and reset_plc_master_secret_online (both with optional portalConfirmations; TIA Portal dialogs of the three issue #16 operations are answered decline (default: No, recorded, the item fails) or accept (Yes, recorded, a warning)): OnlineProvider.SetPlcMasterSecret(SecureString) / ResetPlcMasterSecret() on a PLC that is Online (connect first with plc_tia_online go_online; otherwise state_changed); OnlineControl (read-write and full), acknowledge guard plc_master_secret_online: read-write asks the human for every such call, full runs it under policy; the secret cannot be read back, so the item is notVerified (success false). Actual values of a running PLC (package G; not live-tested): load_snapshot_as_actual_values and load_start_values_as_actual_values (blockPath of a global or instance DB, whose first segment names the PLC; optional portalConfirmations) call ValueService.LoadSnapshotAsActualValues() / LoadStartValuesAsActualValues() of the DB's interface on a PLC that is Online (a real CPU or PLCSIM, connected with plc_tia_online go_online; otherwise state_changed): the DB's stored snapshot (create_db_snapshot) or its start values overwrite its actual values in the controller; OnlineControl, acknowledge guard plc_loads_actual_values_online (read-write asks for every such call, full runs it under policy); actual values are not readable through Openness, so the item is notVerified (success false). Downloads to a controller stay with plc_download (rhTarget primary|backup for an R/H system). Loadable files (issue #26; not live-tested): generate_loadable (filePath, target Plc|PlcSim, exactly one of blockPaths (blocks of the non-unit program, one PLC) or unitNames (software units), optional plcName (default: the PLC the block paths name, else the only PLC) and overwrite): LoadableProvider.GenerateLoadable(FileInfo, IEnumerable<PlcBlock> | IEnumerable<PlcUnit>, TargetOption), the provider found among the PlcSoftware's GetServiceInfos() (not listed: unsupported_capability), the overload and the TargetOption member bound at runtime (missing: api_member_missing; TargetOption.None is documented to throw and is not offered); the file is written next to the target, moved into place without overwriting unless overwrite:true and re-hashed (result sha256, verification check file); a call that writes no file fails postcondition_failed. Project block-compilation settings (project-wide, no plcName, standalone projects only; not live-tested): set_project_compilation_settings (simulationDuringBlockCompilation and/or virtualPlcDuringBlockCompilation, true or false): sets \"Simulation während Bausteinübersetzung unterstützen\" (PlcSimulationSettingsProvider.IsSimulationDuringBlockCompilationEnabled, which Siemens' PLCSIM Advanced getting-started asks for before a Softbus download) and the virtual PLC flag (VirtualPlcSettingsProvider.IsVirtualPlcDuringBlockCompilationEnabled) through Project.GetService<T>(), the providers get_project_status reads as compilationSettings; the write is bound on the live provider (a writable property, else an attribute GetAttributeInfos lists as writable, else api_member_missing with nothing changed), result.settings has before, after, route and signature per setting, and a different read-back fails postcondition_failed (check compilationSettings). File paths are absolute drive or UNC share (\\\\server\\share\\...) paths, checked lexically; device (\\\\?\\, \\\\.\\, \\??\\) and alternate-data-stream paths, reserved device names and segments ending in a space or a dot are refused; a mapped network drive or a link on the way is allowed and reported (info guard plc_file_on_network_or_link). Technology objects (not live-tested; every TO-specific Siemens member is bound at runtime and fails closed with unsupported_capability): create_technology_object (name, technologyType, version, optional folderPath; TechnologicalInstanceDBComposition.Create(name, type, version); the accepted version depends on the CPU firmware (live V21 2026-11-02: a CPU 1516-3 PN/DP FW V2.9 rejected TO_PositioningAxis 10.0 and accepted 6.0) and is never guessed), delete_technology_object, rename_technology_object (newName), create_technology_object_group, delete_technology_object_group and rename_technology_object_group (folderPath; renames need Name listed writable by GetAttributeInfos), set_technology_object_parameter (name, parameterName and value converted to exactly the runtime type of the current value, or tableName and tagName for a PlcTag value; read back with a fresh Find, a different read-back fails postcondition_failed; Actor.* parameter writes do not connect hardware), connect_technology_object_hardware (connectionInterface actor|sensor|torque|measuringInput|outputCam|ident, resolving only the providers that interface needs (sensor: the axis provider first, the encoder provider as the alternative), and connectionKind address|module|modules|channel|tag|dbMember with that overload's fields; verified by reading the interface back: connected, and the overload's documented target property reads the requested target, otherwise postcondition_failed) and disconnect_technology_object_hardware, export_technology_object (filePath, optional overwrite) and import_technology_object (filePath, optional folderPath; overwrite:true imports with ImportOptions.Override) as SimaticML files at absolute drive or UNC share paths (device paths and reserved device names refused; a mapped network drive is used with a warning; an existing export file needs overwrite:true), update_technology_object_content (content and expectedContentHash from get_technology_object_content; Import with ImportOptions.Override). Compile the PLC with compile_check afterwards. CPU protection (offline project, effective after plc_download; passwords only from password sources, never as values, never generated; not live-tested; every member bound at runtime by exact signature, a missing one fails api_member_missing with nothing changed): set_plc_access_level (accessLevel FullAccessIncludingFailsafe, FullAccess, ReadAccess, HMIAccess or NoAccess, optional plcName; resetAccessLevelPasswords [levels] with ResetPassword(level) first, then PlcProtectionAccessLevel, then optional accessLevelPasswords { level: source } with PlcAccessLevelProvider.SetPassword(level, SecureString) (live V21 2026-11-02: TIA Portal accepts a level's password call only while the current level is less open than it, and every level needs its own password; a failed SetPassword restores the level read before); levels more open than accessLevel that the call omits come from the server password map (purpose = level name); before and after are read where readable, a different read-back fails postcondition_failed, an unreadable one is readBack unreadable; a matched read-back is the item's verification, check readBack; result.calls lists every member called, result.passwordSources the source tokens), protect_plc_confidential_data (passwordVariable, the master secret; PlcMasterSecretConfigurator.Protect(SecureString); allConfiguration:true uses ProtectAllPlcConfigurationWithPassword, or ProtectAllPlcConfiguration() without passwordVariable), change_plc_confidential_data_password (passwordVariable current, newPasswordVariable new; ChangePassword(SecureString, SecureString)) and disable_plc_confidential_data_protection (optional plcName; Unprotect(SecureString) with passwordVariable, else Unprotect(); allConfiguration:true calls UnprotectAllPlcConfiguration(); readBack notAvailable, MasterSecretConfiguration is in observedBefore/observedAfter). The confidential-data operations take the map's purpose PlcMasterSecretPassword when passwordVariable is omitted. Lowering protection fires the info guard plc_lowers_cpu_protection, raising it plc_raises_cpu_protection; check the result with compile_check scope hardware. Block know-how and write protection (issue #5, offline project; passwords only from password sources, never as values; not live-tested; providers found among the block's GetServiceInfos() by full name, members bound at runtime, a missing one fails api_member_missing with nothing changed, a provider the block does not offer unsupported_capability): set_block_know_how_protection (blockPath, passwordVariable; PlcBlockProtectionProvider.Protect(SecureString)) and remove_block_know_how_protection (blockPath, passwordVariable the current password; Unprotect(SecureString)), verified by reading PlcBlock.IsKnowHowProtected back; define_block_write_protection (blockPath, passwordVariable; PlcBlockWriteProtectionProvider.Define(SecureString), read back IsDefined), set_block_write_protection and remove_block_write_protection (blockPath, passwordVariable; Protect/Unprotect(SecureString), read back IsProtected) and change_block_write_protection_password (blockPath, passwordVariable current, newPasswordVariable new; Change(SecureString, SecureString), read back IsDefined, the new password itself is not readable). Omitted passwordVariable comes from the server password map (purpose KnowHowProtection or BlockWriteProtection, PLC from blockPath). A password set anew is first checked against the provider's GetInvalidPasswordCharacters() (validation_error, nothing changed; the message never says which character). A readable read-back that differs fails postcondition_failed; a matched one is the verification (check blockProtection), an unreadable one stays trusted. A fail-safe block follows TIA Portal's safety login rule (acceptance guard; login block guard only when a safety password is set and the session is not logged on). Info guards plc_sets_block_protection and plc_lowers_block_protection. Project languages and project texts (issue #8; project-wide, no plcName, standalone projects and local sessions; not live-tested; every member bound at runtime, a missing one fails api_member_missing with nothing changed): set_project_languages (at least one of addLanguages, removeLanguages (culture names, 1-64 each), editingLanguage, referenceLanguage): every culture is resolved with LanguageSettings.Languages.Find(CultureInfo) first (a culture TIA Portal does not support fails target_not_found, nothing changed), then ActiveLanguages.Add(Language) for each addition, ReferenceLanguage and EditingLanguage are set (the V21 reference documents no setter; a non-writable property is api_member_missing), then ActiveLanguages.Remove(Language) for each removal (TIA Portal decides what happens to that language's texts); everything is read back and a mismatch fails postcondition_failed (check projectLanguages; info guard plc_changes_project_languages; add a language before writing texts in it). export_project_texts (filePath ending in .xlsx, sourceLanguage, targetLang